necesidades similares. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros ámbitos. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen según criterios objetivos, como presupuestos cerrados o precios de mercado.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 42 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 7.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.4 to 8.6. December accounts for 14% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 38 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,900 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the spread across many different suppliers do not indicate improper conduct. These patterns could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for unusual frequency and compare awardee A's contracts to others to see if they share commonalities. Review contract [1] to confirm if the amount was near the limit and if it aligns with typical pricing for the service.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["bN%2FUcklFdTLCfVQHDepjGQ%3D%3D","kyY50WUQOP39pbnDwlaUlg%3D%3D","kr%2BRMuPa54rgL1BHd3qjQA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}